---
layout: base.njk
title: "Recipes"
nav: "recipes"
description: "Celiac-safe, gluten-free recipes from Morgan and Allie — breakfast, dinner, and dessert, all tested in their own kitchens."
permalink: "recipes/index.html"
---
<section class="page-header">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Recipes</span>
    <h1>Gluten-free recipes we actually make on repeat</h1>
    <p class="lead">Every recipe here is naturally gluten-free or made with certified gluten-free ingredients. Always double-check your specific brands — see our note on cross-contact below.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="callout callout-warn">
      <h4>Before you cook: read the labels</h4>
      <p style="margin:0;">"Gluten-free" ingredients can still cross-contaminate at home. Use certified gluten-free oats, flour, baking powder, and soy sauce/tamari, and keep a dedicated GF toaster, colander, and cutting board if anyone else in your kitchen eats regular wheat products.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% for recipe in collections.recipes %}
<section class="{% if loop.index is even %}section-alt{% endif %}">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="card" style="max-width:900px; margin:0 auto;">
      {% if recipe.data.photo %}<img class="card-photo" src="{{ recipe.data.photo }}" alt="{{ recipe.data.title }}" style="height:220px;">{% endif %}
      <div class="card-body">
        <span class="tag tag-dedicated">{{ recipe.data.category }}</span>
        <h2 style="margin-top:6px;">{{ recipe.data.title }}</h2>
        {{ recipe.templateContent | safe }}
        <div class="recipe-meta">
          <div><strong>Prep</strong>{{ recipe.data.prep_time }}</div>
          <div><strong>Cook</strong>{{ recipe.data.cook_time }}</div>
          <div><strong>Serves</strong>{{ recipe.data.serves }}</div>
        </div>
        <div class="recipe-columns">
          <div>
            <h3>Ingredients</h3>
            <ul>
              {% for i in recipe.data.ingredients %}<li>{{ i }}</li>{% endfor %}
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Instructions</h3>
            <ol>
              {% for step in recipe.data.instructions %}<li>{{ step }}</li>{% endfor %}
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{% endfor %}

<section>
  <div class="container" style="text-align:center;">
    <h2>Want new recipes in your inbox?</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="margin:0 auto 24px;">We share a new recipe in almost every newsletter issue.</p>
    <a href="/newsletter/#subscribe" class="btn btn-primary">Subscribe to the Newsletter</a>
  </div>
</section>
